11.4.2 The Partition Creation Visitor
The partition creation visitor class PCVisitor is also a child class of the
base class NodeVisitor and is used to extract a partition from a hierarchical
clustering. Listing 11.17 shows the declaration of the class.
Class PCVisitor depends on class CVisitor, which is used to create a
cluster from a subtree of a hierarchical clustering. The class creates a cluster
by including all the leaf nodes of the subtree.
